defmodule <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows do
  @moduledoc """
  What the page and reusable-element workflows scaffolded from Bubble run
  on (WTF-372): the LiveView glue the pages call (`mount/2`,
  `handle_params/3`, `handle_event/4`, `handle_info/3`) and the step
  helpers the generated bodies call (`<Page>Live.Workflows`,
  `<%= @web %>.Reusables.<Name>.Workflows`).

  ## Events

  A browser can only ask the page to run what the page lists
  (`__bubble__(:surface)` of its `Workflows` module and of the reusable
  elements it renders, `__bubble__(:instances)`): a click (`bubble:click`)
  or an input change (`bubble:change`, `bubble:commit`) of an element the
  page renders in a scope (reusable-element instance) it renders. Anything else is ignored.

  A reusable instance in a repeating group's cell (WTF-494,
  `__bubble__(:cells)`) has a scope per cell, the cell's thing's
  (`<%= @web %>.Bubble.cell_scope/4`): the page lists the scopes of the
  cells it read (`<%= @web %>.BubbleData`, as the current user), and an
  event in any other scope is ignored, so a browser can only reach the
  cells of things the user was shown. Its workflows run in that scope (its
  custom states, inputs and data are the cell's); its page-load,
  condition-true and "do every" workflows do not run in a cell.
  Event parameters never become atoms, never name a workflow, a module or a
  record: the page looks the element up in its own static lists and runs
  the workflows listed there, with the values it keeps (current user,
  custom states, input values, URL parameters). Input values are text,
  numbers or yes/no, never records.

  A click runs the workflows of the element clicked only (LiveView's
  `phx-click`), in Bubble ID order; Bubble also runs those of a clickable
  element around it (unverified). A workflow run in the browser (element
  steps only) never reaches the server.

  Typing in a text or multiline input (WTF-475) reaches the page 300 ms
  after the last keystroke (`phx-debounce`): its value for the page's
  data, which reads again only the sources that read it, and for
  conditions. Its "An input's value is changed" workflows run when it is
  committed, on blur (`bubble:commit`), once per value that differs from
  the one last committed or set by a workflow; Enter is a change. The
  input shows the value the page keeps, so a re-render never puts back
  its first value. Checkboxes,
  dropdowns and the other inputs commit on every change.

  ## Running a workflow

  A workflow starts only if it and every workflow it calls or schedules
  (custom events, backend workflows), transitively, were lowered
  completely: `blocked` in its module's `__bubble__(:workflows)` (the
  residue subjects and blocked callees bubble_ex found, as the backend's
  `not_lowered`) makes it refuse **before its first step** and log an
  error. The same holds for data access (below). When a click or an input
  change is refused, the page also shows a short notice, "This action
  isn't available yet." (WTF-453, the page hook's `bubble:notice`, a polite
  live region): never the workflow, its reason or any ID, which stay in
  the log. Steps run in Bubble order; a step's "Only when"
  skips it; a failing step ends the workflow (steps before it keep their
  effects, as in Bubble). Custom states, input values, element steps and
  navigation apply to the page when the event's workflows end. The first
  page-leaving navigation of an event (another page, a reload, a URL, log
  out) wins, in a later step or a later workflow (in Bubble the page is
  gone once one runs); a same-page one (a URL parameter) never blocks
  another. Bubble does not guarantee the order of workflows on the same
  trigger, and neither does this.
  "Terminate this workflow" ends it; a custom event's return values are
  its caller's step result.

  "Add a pause before next action" (WTF-451) never blocks the page: the
  event ends there (what the steps before it did applies to the page) and
  the rest of the workflow, and of every custom event waiting on it, runs
  in a message the page sends itself after the pause
  (`Process.send_after/3`), with the step results, arguments and start time
  it had. A pause lasts at most `:max_pause_ms` (default 60_000); it costs
  one call of the run's call budget and continues the run's budgets one
  link further down the chain, as a scheduled custom event, so a workflow
  pausing in a loop ends. Paused work lives in the LiveView process:
  leaving the page (a "Go to page" to another page), closing it or a
  reconnect (LiveView mounts a new process) drops what was still paused.
  A page holds at most `:max_pending` (default 100) paused workflows and
  scheduled custom events at once; beyond that the new ones are dropped,
  logged, and the page shows the refusal notice.

  ## Data access (opt-in)

<%= if @enforced? do %>  The Ash resources have the privacy policies compiled from Bubble
  (`privacy: :enforced`, WTF-423): a workflow reads what the privacy
  rules let the current user read, and its writes are allowed as in Bubble
  (its own conditions guard them; **writes are not checked against the
  privacy rules**). The actor is the current user read afresh with what
  the policies read (`<%= @module %>.Privacy.load_actor/1`) at every event
  and page load. Workflows that read or write stored data (data steps,
  relationship loads, scheduled backend workflows) still run only when
  data access is enabled:<% else %>  The Ash resources are generated with `privacy: :omit`: **no resource has
  an authorizer**, so a workflow that reads or writes stored data would do
  it for anyone who can open the page, on any record. Such workflows (data
  steps, relationship loads, scheduled backend workflows) run only when
  data access is enabled:<% end %>

      config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows, data_access: true

  Without it they refuse to start and log an error. Data steps and
  schedules run on the backend workflow runtime
  (`<%= @module %>.Workflows.Runtime`, WTF-373) with the current user as
  the actor: its stamps, job budget (`:max_jobs`) and call budget
  (`:max_calls`, custom events included) apply. A browser event (a click,
  an input change, page load, a "do every" tick) is a root run with whole
  budgets; a scheduled custom event continues the budgets of the run that
  scheduled it (shared among everything that run scheduled, one call per
  schedule), and a chain of them stops at `:max_chain`, so a
  self-scheduling event ends. The condition-true workflows an event's
  effects fire run within that event's budgets and chain, never fresh
  ones, so a loop through a condition (a workflow that flips a state and
  schedules one that flips it back) ends too. <%= if @enforced? do %>Its `authorize?: true` applies the
  privacy policies.<% else %>Its `authorize?: true` authorizes nothing
  until you add policies.<% end %>

  A browser can trigger any workflow of an element the page lists, visible
  or not: visibility is not part of the allowlist; "Only when" conditions
  are evaluated on the server. An input value above `:max_input_bytes`
  (`config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows`, default 100_000) is
  ignored.

  ## Unverified Bubble behavior

  To confirm by replay (WTF-358): "Reset relevant inputs" resets the inputs
  of the triggering element's container; a condition-true workflow whose
  "run this" is unset runs once per page load; a condition true when the
  page loads fires; "Go to page" lets the workflow finish before the page
  changes; workflows triggered together run one after the other; a custom
  event's caller waits for the custom event's pauses; data sent to the
  index page is at `/index/<unique id>`; a search reading a text input
  updates while the user types, after a pause (about 300 ms here), and
  the input's "An input's value is changed" fires on blur, not on that
  pause (Bubble's manual; WTF-475).
  """

  require Logger

  import Phoenix.Component, only: [assign: 3]

  import Phoenix.LiveView,
    only: [connected?: 1, push_event: 3, push_navigate: 2, push_patch: 2, redirect: 2]

  alias <%= @module %>.Workflows.Runtime
  alias <%= @web %>.Bubble
  alias <%= @web %>.BubbleData

  @max_rounds 10
  @max_input_bytes Application.compile_env(:<%= @app %>, [__MODULE__, :max_input_bytes], 100_000)
  @max_depth 100

  # What a browser is told when its click or input change is refused: no
  # workflow, reason or ID (those are logged).
  @refused_notice "This action isn't available yet."

  defmodule Ctx do
    @moduledoc """
    The state a workflow runs with: the surface module and instance
    `scope`, the actor, the start time, its arguments and step results, the
    page's custom states, input values (and their `first` values) and URL,
    what it asks of the page (element steps `js`, `navigate`, delayed
    `messages`), and the backend runtime's context of the event (`backend`,
    `<%= @module %>.Workflows.Runtime.root/2`: its job and call budgets).
    The page's data (WTF-420, `<%= @web %>.BubbleData`): what it loaded
    (`data`), the unique ID of its thing from the URL (`thing`) and, while
    a repeating group's cells are read, the current cell's thing and
    1-based index (`cell`, `cell_index`), and `batch` while the cells (or
    the instances in cells, WTF-494) are read together; `data_stale` once a data step
    ran (it may have written what the page shows). `page_path` is the
    page's own path (without its thing's segment) and `takes_thing`
    whether the page reads a thing from its URL (WTF-454); `resume` the
    step a paused workflow continues from (WTF-451). `displayed` is what
    "Display data" steps showed (WTF-492), by `{scope, element}` (and cell
    index): `{resource, list?, value}`, a thing as its unique ID.
    """
    defstruct [
      :module,
      :workflow,
      :actor,
      :now,
      :returns,
      :navigate,
      :backend,
      :thing,
      :cell,
      :cell_index,
      :resume,
      batch: false,
      scope: "",
      path: "/",
      page_path: "/",
      takes_thing: false,
      args: %{},
      steps: %{},
      states: %{},
      inputs: %{},
      url: %{},
      data: %{},
      displayed: %{},
      first: %{},
      js: [],
      messages: [],
      depth: 0,
      data_stale: false
    ]

    @type t :: %__MODULE__{}
  end

  # --- LiveView glue -------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Assigns the page's custom states (defaults) and input values (first
  values) for the page and every reusable-element instance it renders, and
  once connected, schedules its page-loaded workflows. It reads the
  current user for this page load (<%= if @enforced? do %>the actor, with data access on, and <% end %>the user as the visibility
  conditionals see them, WTF-501) and loads no data (`handle_params/4`
  does, WTF-420).
  """
  def mount(socket, page) do
    surfaces = surfaces(page)

    states =
      for {scope, module} <- surfaces,
          {{element, state}, value} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).states,
          into: %{},
          do: {{scope, element, state}, value}

    inputs =
      for {scope, module} <- surfaces,
          {element, {_type, value}} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).inputs,
          into: %{},
          do: {{scope, element}, value}

    if connected?(socket) do
      send(self(), {:bubble, :page_loaded})

      for {scope, module} <- surfaces,
          {id, seconds} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).intervals,
          is_number(seconds) and seconds > 0,
          do: :timer.send_interval(clamp(seconds, 100), {:bubble, :interval, scope, id})
    end

    socket
    |> assign(:bubble_states, states)
    |> assign(:bubble_inputs, inputs)
    |> assign(:bubble_first_inputs, inputs)
    |> assign(:bubble_url, %{})
    |> assign(:bubble_path, "/")
    |> assign(:bubble_page_path, "/")
    |> assign(:bubble_takes_thing, false)
    |> assign(:bubble_refused, false)
    |> assign(:bubble_pending_messages, 0)
    |> assign(:bubble_conditions, %{})
    |> assign(:bubble_data, %{})
    |> assign(:bubble_data_stale, false)
    |> assign(:bubble_data_inputs, MapSet.new())
    |> assign(:bubble_displayed, %{})
    |> assign(:bubble_cells, [])
    |> assign(:bubble_committed, %{})
    |> assign(:bubble_thing, nil)<%= if @enforced? do %>
    |> then(&if(BubbleData.data_access?(), do: refresh_actor(&1), else: &1))<% end %>
    |> refresh_viewer()
    |> assign(:bubble_mounted, true)
  end

  @doc """
  A disconnected LiveView socket with `page`'s states and inputs (no page
  load, no timers), for tests: pass it to `handle_event/4` and
  `handle_info/3`.
  """
  def socket(page, path \\ "/") do
    %Phoenix.LiveView.Socket{}
    |> mount(page)
    |> handle_params(%{}, "http://localhost" <> path)
  end

  @doc """
  Keeps the URL's path and query parameters (text only), and the page's
  own path: the path without its thing's segment when the route has one.
  """
  def handle_params(socket, params, uri) do
    url =
      for {k, v} <- params,
          is_binary(k) and is_binary(v) and k != "bubble_thing",
          into: %{},
          do: {k, v}

    %URI{path: path, host: host} = URI.parse(uri)
    path = path || "/"

    socket
    |> assign(:bubble_url, url)
    |> assign(:bubble_path, path)
    |> assign(:bubble_page_path, page_path(socket, params, path, host))
  end

  @doc """
  As `handle_params/3`, then keeps the unique ID of the page's thing from
  the URL path (a Bubble ID, else none) and loads the page's data
  (`<%= @web %>.BubbleData`, WTF-420).

  The current user (<%= if @enforced? do %>the actor, and <% end %>the user as the visibility
  conditionals see them) is read afresh, unless `mount/2` has just read
  it for this very page load (WTF-501): the first `handle_params` after a
  mount, never a later one (a patch, a URL parameter). A connected mount's page-loaded
  workflows run on the data this load read<%= if @enforced? do %>, as the actor read again<% end %> (`handle_info/3`).
  """
  def handle_params(socket, page, params, uri) do
    mounted? = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_mounted, false)

    socket =
      if mounted?,
        do: socket,
        else: socket<%= if @enforced? do %>
          |> refresh_actor()<% end %>
          |> refresh_viewer()

    socket
    |> assign(:bubble_mounted, false)
    |> assign(:bubble_load_fresh, mounted? and connected?(socket))
    |> handle_params(params, uri)
    |> assign(:bubble_thing, BubbleData.thing_id(params, URI.parse(uri).path))
    |> assign(:bubble_takes_thing, takes_thing?(page))
    |> BubbleData.load(page, actor_fresh?: true)
  end

  # The page's own path. When the router took `bubble_thing` from the
  # path (a `/<page>/:bubble_thing` route, never a query parameter of the
  # same name), the route without that segment; the index page's
  # `/index/:bubble_thing` is `/` (a bare `/index` has no route).
  # The router's own report decides, never `params`' value: a
  # percent-encoded segment (`%2F%2Fevil.example`) decodes differently.
  defp page_path(socket, %{"bubble_thing" => _}, path, host) do
    router = socket.router || <%= @web %>.Router

    case Phoenix.Router.route_info(router, "GET", path, host) do
      %{route: route, path_params: %{"bubble_thing" => _}} when is_binary(route) ->
        case String.replace_suffix(route, "/:bubble_thing", "") do
          ^route -> path
          "/index" -> "/"
          "" -> "/"
          base -> base
        end

      _ ->
        path
    end
  end

  defp page_path(_socket, _params, path, _host), do: path

  # Whether the page reads its thing from its `/:bubble_thing` segment
  # (WTF-420); every page is routed with one, the others ignore it (WTF-466).
  defp takes_thing?(page),
    do: Enum.any?(BubbleData.sources(page), &match?(%{read: :url_thing, fun: f} when f != nil, &1))

  @doc "Runs the workflows of a click or an input change the page lists."
  def handle_event(socket, page, "bubble:click", %{"scope" => scope, "element" => element})
      when is_binary(scope) and is_binary(element) do
    with {:ok, module} <- surface(socket, page, scope),
         [_ | _] = ids <- Map.get(module.__bubble__(:surface).clicks, element, []) do
      socket = assign(socket, :bubble_refused, false)
      {:noreply, socket |> event(page, [{module, scope, ids, %{}}]) |> notice()}
    else
      _ -> {:noreply, socket}
    end
  end

  # A text input's change (`"on" => "blur"`, sent while typing or on
  # Enter) is its value for the page's data and conditions only; its
  # workflows run when it is committed (`bubble:commit`, on blur). Any
  # other input's change commits it.
  def handle_event(socket, page, "bubble:change", %{"bubble" => %{} = params}) do
    with {:ok, module, scope, element, value} <- input_event(socket, page, params) do
      socket = assign(socket, :bubble_refused, false) |> put_input(scope, element, value)

      if Map.get(params, "on") == "blur" do
        {:noreply, socket |> event(page, [], nil, :deferred) |> notice()}
      else
        commit(socket, page, module, scope, element, value)
      end
    else
      _ -> {:noreply, socket}
    end
  end

  # A text input committed on blur (`phx-blur`: the scope, empty on the
  # page itself, and the element as values). Its workflows run when its
  # value differs from the one last committed (or set by a workflow).
  def handle_event(socket, page, "bubble:commit", %{} = params) do
    params = Map.put_new(params, "scope", "")

    with {:ok, module, scope, element, value} <- input_event(socket, page, params) do
      socket = assign(socket, :bubble_refused, false) |> put_input(scope, element, value)
      commit(socket, page, module, scope, element, value)
    else
      _ -> {:noreply, socket}
    end
  end

  def handle_event(socket, _page, _event, _params), do: {:noreply, socket}

  defp input_event(socket, page, params) do
    with %{"scope" => scope, "element" => element} when is_binary(scope) and is_binary(element) <-
           params,
         {:ok, module} <- surface(socket, page, scope),
         %{^element => {type, _first}} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).inputs,
         {:ok, value} <- coerce(type, Map.get(params, "value")) do
      {:ok, module, scope, element, value}
    end
  end

  # The input's new value; the sources reading it read again (WTF-475).
  defp put_input(socket, scope, element, value) do
    if Map.get(socket.assigns.bubble_inputs, {scope, element}) == value do
      socket
    else
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_inputs, Map.put(socket.assigns.bubble_inputs, {scope, element}, value))
      |> BubbleData.mark_inputs([element])
    end
  end

  defp commit(socket, page, module, scope, element, value) do
    key = {scope, element}
    committed = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_committed) || %{}
    before = Map.get(committed, key, Map.get(socket.assigns.bubble_first_inputs, key))
    socket = assign(socket, :bubble_committed, Map.put(committed, key, value))

    runs =
      case Map.get(module.__bubble__(:surface).changes, element, []) do
        ids when ids != [] and before != value -> [{module, scope, ids, %{}}]
        _ -> []
      end

    {:noreply, socket |> event(page, runs, nil, :deferred) |> notice()}
  end

  @doc "Page loaded, delayed custom events and \"do every\" workflows."
  def handle_info(socket, page, {:bubble, :page_loaded}) do
    runs =
      for {scope, module} <- surfaces(page),
          do: {module, scope, module.__bubble__(:surface).loaded, %{}}

    # Sent from a connected mount: handle_params/4 has loaded the data
    # already. The page-load workflows and conditions run on that load; a
    # workflow that changes it marks it stale and the page reads again.
    # Its workflows may write: they run as the current user read afresh
    # (WTF-501); the viewer the load rendered with is kept, unless
    # anything ran since (a patch's own handle_params read it again).
    fresh? = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_load_fresh, false)
    socket = assign(socket, :bubble_load_fresh, false)
    {:noreply, event(socket, page, runs, nil, if(fresh?, do: :mount_loaded, else: :already_loaded))}
  end

  def handle_info(socket, page, {:bubble, :run, scope, module, id, args, budget}) do
    socket = delivered(socket)

    if surface(socket, page, scope) == {:ok, module} and budget?(budget),
      do: {:noreply, event(socket, page, [{module, scope, [id], args}], cap_budget(budget))},
      else: {:noreply, socket}
  end

  # Marks the data stale and coalesces a burst of changes into one read;
  # ignores notifications for other pages' topics.
  def handle_info(socket, _page, {:bubble, :data_changed, topic}) when is_binary(topic),
    do: {:noreply, BubbleData.changed(socket, topic)}

  def handle_info(socket, page, {:bubble, :data_refresh, ref}) do
    if BubbleData.pending?(socket, ref) do<%= if @enforced? do %>
      socket = refresh_actor(socket)<% end %>
      socket = refresh_viewer(socket)
      run = socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_run] || start(socket, nil)

      socket =
        socket
        |> assign(:bubble_pending_run, nil)
        |> assign(:bubble_refused, false)
        |> BubbleData.refresh(page, ref, actor_fresh?: true)

      # The pending events are input changes: a refused one gets its notice.
      pending = socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_events] || []
      {socket, run} = run_events(socket, page, pending, run)
      socket = socket |> assign(:bubble_pending_events, nil) |> assign(:bubble_pending_keys, nil)
      {socket, run} = settle_after_events(socket, page, pending, run)
      {:noreply, socket |> dispatch(run) |> notice()}
    else
      {:noreply, socket}
    end
  end

  # The rest of a paused workflow (WTF-451), sent by the page itself.
  def handle_info(socket, page, {:bubble, :resume, frames, now, budget}) do
    socket = delivered(socket)

    cond do
      not (well_formed?(frames) and budget?(budget) and match?(%DateTime{}, now)) ->
        Logger.warning("bubble: a malformed paused workflow was ignored")
        {:noreply, socket}

      resumable?(socket, page, frames) ->
        {:noreply, event(socket, page, [{:resume, frames, now}], cap_budget(budget))}

      true ->
        # Its instance is no longer on the page (a cell whose thing left
        # the list, WTF-494): what was left of it is dropped.
        Logger.info("bubble: a paused workflow's instance is no longer on the page; it was dropped")
        {:noreply, socket}
    end
  end

  def handle_info(socket, page, {:bubble, :interval, scope, id}) do
    case surface(socket, page, scope) do
      {:ok, module} -> {:noreply, event(socket, page, [{module, scope, [id], %{}}])}
      _ -> {:noreply, socket}
    end
  end

  def handle_info(socket, _page, _message), do: {:noreply, socket}

<%= if @enforced? do %>  @doc """
  Reads the current user afresh with what the privacy policies read
  (`<%= @module %>.Privacy.load_actor/1`) into `@bubble_actor`: the actor of
  every read and write of this event or page load, so a changed role is
  never served stale.
  """
  def refresh_actor(socket),
    do: assign(socket, :bubble_actor, <%= @module %>.Privacy.load_actor(socket.assigns[:current_user]))

  @doc "The actor of the page's reads and workflows (`refresh_actor/1`)."
  def current_actor(socket) do
    case Map.fetch(socket.assigns, :bubble_actor) do
      {:ok, actor} -> actor
      :error -> <%= @module %>.Privacy.load_actor(socket.assigns[:current_user])
    end
  end

<% end %>  @doc """
  Reads the current user as the page's visibility conditionals see it
  (WTF-477) into `@bubble_viewer`, at mount, every page load and event: a
  changed role is never served stale.<%= if @viewer? do %> Read with the user as the actor<%= if @enforced? do %>,
  so the privacy rules apply: a field the user may not view reads as
  empty (nil), as in Bubble<% end %>; the relationships the conditionals read
  (`Bubble.viewer_loads/0`) are loaded with data access on and empty
  without it. Nil when logged out; when the user may not read their own
  record, only their ID (logged in, every field empty).<% else %> No
  visibility conditional reads the user: the session's, read nowhere.<% end %>
  """
<%= if @viewer? do %>  def refresh_viewer(socket), do: assign(socket, :bubble_viewer, viewer(socket))

  defp viewer(socket) do
    case socket.assigns[:current_user] do
      nil ->
        nil

      %{id: id} ->
        actor = <%= if @enforced? do %>current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>
        resource = <%= @module %>.Accounts.Resources.user()

        case Ash.get(resource, id, actor: actor, not_found_error?: false) do
          {:ok, %{} = viewer} -> viewer |> viewer_loads(actor) |> unforbidden()
          _ -> resource |> struct(id: id) |> empty_loads(Bubble.viewer_loads())
        end
    end
  end

  defp viewer_loads(viewer, actor) do<%= if @viewer_loads? do %>
    if BubbleData.data_access?(),
      do: BubbleData.load_value(viewer, Bubble.viewer_loads(), %{actor: actor}),
      else: empty_loads(viewer, Bubble.viewer_loads())<% else %>
    _ = actor
    viewer<% end %>
  end

  # Relationships not read read as empty, never as `%Ash.NotLoaded{}`.
  defp empty_loads(record, loads) do
    Enum.reduce(loads, record, fn [name | _], acc ->
      key = String.to_existing_atom(name)

      if match?(%Ash.NotLoaded{}, Map.get(acc, key)), do: Map.put(acc, key, nil), else: acc
    end)
  end

  defp unforbidden(%Ash.ForbiddenField{}), do: nil
  defp unforbidden(list) when is_list(list), do: Enum.map(list, &unforbidden/1)

  defp unforbidden(%{__struct__: module} = record) do
    if Ash.Resource.Info.resource?(module),
      do:
        Enum.reduce(Map.from_struct(record), record, fn {k, v}, acc ->
          Map.put(acc, k, unforbidden(v))
        end),
      else: record
  end

  defp unforbidden(value), do: value
<% else %>  def refresh_viewer(socket), do: assign(socket, :bubble_viewer, socket.assigns[:current_user])
<% end %>
  @doc """
  The page itself (scope \"\") and the reusable-element instances it
  renders outside repeating group cells.
  """
  def surfaces(page), do: [{"", page} | page.__bubble__(:instances)]

  @doc """
  As `surfaces/1`, with the reusable instances in the cells the page read
  last (WTF-494, `put_cells/2`): one scope per cell.
  """
  def surfaces(socket, page), do: surfaces(page) ++ cell_surfaces(socket)

  defp cell_surfaces(socket), do: Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_cells) || []

  @doc """
  The reusable instances a surface module renders once per cell of a
  repeating group (WTF-494): `{repeating group, [{scope relative to the
  cell's, module}]}`; none for a module scaffolded before it.
  """
  def cells(module) do
    module.__bubble__(:cells)
  rescue
    FunctionClauseError -> []
  end

  # The surface of an event's scope: the page, an instance it renders, or
  # an instance in a cell it read (never a scope the browser made up).
  defp surface(_socket, page, ""), do: {:ok, page}

  defp surface(socket, page, scope) do
    case List.keyfind(page.__bubble__(:instances), scope, 0) ||
           List.keyfind(cell_surfaces(socket), scope, 0) do
      {^scope, module} -> {:ok, module}
      nil -> :error
    end
  end

  @doc """
  Keeps the reusable instances in cells the page just read (WTF-494,
  `{scope, module}`), with their custom states' defaults and their
  inputs' first values for the cells new to the page (a cell the page
  already showed keeps its own). What the page kept for a cell no longer
  read (its thing left the list, or the user may no longer read it) is
  dropped: its states, inputs and what "Display data" showed in it.
  """
  def put_cells(socket, cells) do
    gone =
      socket.assigns
      |> Map.get(:bubble_cells, [])
      |> Enum.map(&elem(&1, 0))
      |> MapSet.new()
      |> MapSet.difference(MapSet.new(cells, &elem(&1, 0)))

    states =
      for {scope, module} <- cells,
          {{element, state}, value} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).states,
          reduce: drop_scopes(socket.assigns.bubble_states, gone) do
        acc -> Map.put_new(acc, {scope, element, state}, value)
      end

    inputs =
      for {scope, module} <- cells,
          {element, {_type, value}} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).inputs,
          do: {{scope, element}, value}

    socket
    |> assign(:bubble_cells, cells)
    |> assign(:bubble_states, states)
    |> assign(:bubble_inputs, put_new(drop_scopes(socket.assigns.bubble_inputs, gone), inputs))
    |> assign(:bubble_first_inputs, put_new(drop_scopes(socket.assigns.bubble_first_inputs, gone), inputs))
    |> assign(:bubble_committed, drop_scopes(Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_committed) || %{}, gone))
    |> assign(:bubble_displayed, drop_scopes(Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_displayed) || %{}, gone))
  end

  defp put_new(map, pairs), do: Enum.reduce(pairs, map, fn {k, v}, acc -> Map.put_new(acc, k, v) end)

  # A map keyed by tuples whose first element is a scope, without `gone`'s.
  defp drop_scopes(map, gone) do
    if MapSet.size(gone) == 0,
      do: map,
      else: Map.reject(map, fn {key, _} -> MapSet.member?(gone, elem(key, 0)) end)
  end

  defp budget?(%{jobs: j, calls: c, chain: n}),
    do: is_integer(j) and j >= 0 and is_integer(c) and c >= 0 and is_integer(n) and n >= 0

  defp budget?(_), do: false

  # A budget never above a root run's (`:max_jobs`, `:max_calls`,
  # `:max_chain`).
  defp cap_budget(%{jobs: jobs, calls: calls, chain: chain}) do
    root = Runtime.root(nil, nil)
    %{jobs: min(jobs, root.budget), calls: min(calls, root.calls), chain: min(chain, max_chain())}
  end

  # Every paused workflow is well formed (every one but the innermost waits
  # on a call), and belongs to a surface the page renders, in its scope.
  defp well_formed?([_ | outer] = frames) when is_list(outer),
    do: Enum.all?(frames, &frame?/1) and Enum.all?(outer, &is_binary(&1.call))

  defp well_formed?(_frames), do: false

  defp resumable?(socket, page, frames),
    do: Enum.all?(frames, &(surface(socket, page, &1.scope) == {:ok, &1.module}))

  defp frame?(%{module: module, scope: scope, workflow: id, at: at, args: args, steps: steps, call: call} = frame)
       when is_atom(module) and is_binary(scope) and is_binary(id) and is_integer(at) and at > 0 and
              is_map(args) and is_map(steps) and (is_nil(call) or is_binary(call)) and
              is_map_key(frame, :returns),
       do: true

  defp frame?(_frame), do: false

  # One paused workflow or scheduled custom event was delivered.
  defp delivered(socket),
    do: assign(socket, :bubble_pending_messages, max(Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_pending_messages, 0) - 1, 0))

  defp max_pending do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_pending, 100) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n >= 0 -> n
      _ -> 100
    end
  end

  # Tells the browser its click or input change was refused (`@refused_notice`).
  defp notice(socket) do
    if socket.assigns[:bubble_refused] do
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_refused, false)
      |> push_event("bubble:notice", %{text: @refused_notice})
    else
      socket
    end
  end

  # Input values are capped (`:max_input_bytes`, default 100_000): a larger
  # one is ignored, as the input's change never happened.
  defp coerce(_type, value) when is_binary(value) and byte_size(value) > @max_input_bytes,
    do: :error

  defp coerce(:text, value) when is_binary(value), do: {:ok, value}
  defp coerce(:text, nil), do: {:ok, nil}
  defp coerce(:boolean, value), do: {:ok, value == "true"}

  defp coerce(:number, value) when is_binary(value) do
    case String.trim(value) do
      "" ->
        {:ok, nil}

      text ->
        case Integer.parse(text) do
          {n, ""} ->
            {:ok, n}

          _ ->
            case Float.parse(text) do
              {n, ""} -> {:ok, n}
              _ -> {:ok, nil}
            end
        end
    end
  end

  defp coerce(:number, nil), do: {:ok, nil}
  defp coerce(_type, _value), do: :error

  # --- running events --------------------------------------------------------------------

  # One event: a browser event (a click, an input change, page load, a "do
  # every" tick) or a scheduled custom event, then the condition-true
  # workflows its effects fire (settle/4), transitively. All of it is one
  # run of the backend runtime: a browser event starts a root run (whole
  # budgets, chain 0), a scheduled custom event continues the budget and
  # chain of the run that scheduled it (WTF-421: the condition-true
  # workflows it fires inherit them too, never fresh ones). What the run
  # scheduled is sent when it ends, sharing what the run left.
  #
  # The page's data is read again only when it is stale
  # (`@bubble_data_stale`: a data step ran, a custom state or an input
  # changed, or a change notification of a record it shows arrived), before
  # a workflow and before conditions settle; every read clears it. An event
  # that changes none of that reads nothing.
  defp event(socket, page, runs, budget \\ nil, reload \\ :immediate) do
    # A deferred event with page data only queues its workflows: the
    # debounced read reads the current user (once) and runs them.
    queued? =
      reload == :deferred and BubbleData.data_access?() and
        Enum.any?(surfaces(page), fn {_, m} -> BubbleData.sources(m) != [] end)

    # A connected mount's page load (`:mount_loaded`) reads the actor
    # afresh (its workflows may write) and keeps the viewer its
    # handle_params/4 has just read (WTF-501).
<%= if @enforced? do %>
    socket = if queued?, do: socket, else: refresh_actor(socket)<% end %>
    socket = if queued? or reload == :mount_loaded, do: socket, else: refresh_viewer(socket)
    run = start(socket, budget)

    case reload do
      loaded when loaded in [:already_loaded, :mount_loaded] ->
        {socket, run} = run_events(socket, page, runs, run)
        {socket, run} = settle_after_events(socket, page, runs, run)
        dispatch(socket, run)

      :deferred ->
        # With page data, input workflows must read the latest input's
        # sources, not the preceding render. Keep their shared run budget
        # until the last keystroke's single debounced read.
        if queued? do
          run = merge_pending(socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_run], run)

          # The same workflows queued with the same input values run once;
          # a commit of another value runs again (WTF-475).
          {pending, keys} =
            Enum.reduce(
              runs,
              {socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_events] || [],
               socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_keys] || MapSet.new()},
              fn {module, scope, ids, _} = entry, {acc, keys} ->
                key = {module, scope, ids, socket.assigns.bubble_inputs}

                if MapSet.member?(keys, key),
                  do: {acc, keys},
                  else: {acc ++ [entry], MapSet.put(keys, key)}
              end
            )

          socket
          |> assign(:bubble_pending_run, run)
          |> assign(:bubble_pending_events, pending)
          |> assign(:bubble_pending_keys, keys)
          |> BubbleData.defer()
        else
          # No page data to re-read: keep input-only workflows and their
          # conditions responsive without a needless debounce timer.
          {socket, run} = run_events(socket, page, runs, run)
          {socket, run} = settle_after_events(socket, page, runs, run)
          dispatch(socket, run)
        end

      :immediate ->
        # A click while an input read is pending flushes its workflows
        # first with the latest inputs, on the same (bounded) run.
        run = merge_pending(socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_run], run)
        pending = (socket.assigns[:bubble_pending_events] || []) ++ runs

        socket =
          socket
          |> assign(:bubble_pending_run, nil)
          |> assign(:bubble_pending_events, nil)
          |> assign(:bubble_pending_keys, nil)
          |> assign(:bubble_data_refresh, nil)

        {socket, run} = run_events(socket, page, pending, run)
        {socket, run} = settle_after_events(socket, page, pending, run)
        dispatch(socket, run)
    end
  end

  # The final workflow may write the data a condition reads. Re-read (when
  # stale) before settling, not later via PubSub (which would start a fresh
  # root budget); the write's own notification is covered by that read.
  defp settle_after_events(socket, page, _runs, run),
    do: settle(BubbleData.reload(socket, page), page, run)

  # Each workflow runs on current data: re-read first when a preceding one
  # (or anything since the last read) made it stale.
  defp run_events(socket, page, runs, run) do
    Enum.reduce(runs, {socket, run}, fn
      {:resume, frames, now}, {socket, run} ->
        socket |> BubbleData.reload(page) |> resume_event(frames, now, run)

      {module, scope, ids, args}, acc ->
        Enum.reduce(ids, acc, fn id, {socket, run} ->
          socket |> BubbleData.reload(page) |> run_event(module, scope, [id], args, run)
        end)
    end)
  end

  defp merge_pending(nil, run), do: run

  defp merge_pending(previous, run) do
    %{run | jobs: min(previous.jobs, run.jobs), calls: min(previous.calls, run.calls),
      chain: max(previous.chain, run.chain), messages: previous.messages ++ run.messages}
  end

  # The budgets of an event: a root run's, or the scheduling run's.
  defp start(socket, budget) do
    root = Runtime.root(nil, <%= if @enforced? do %>current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>)

    case budget do
      %{jobs: jobs, calls: calls, chain: chain} ->
        %{jobs: jobs, calls: calls, chain: chain, messages: []}

      nil ->
        %{jobs: root.budget, calls: root.calls, chain: root.chain, messages: []}
    end
  end

  # What the event scheduled, sent now: each scheduled custom event gets an
  # equal share of what the event left, one link further down the chain,
  # so the total never grows and a self-scheduling chain ends.
  defp dispatch(socket, %{messages: []}), do: socket

  defp dispatch(socket, run) do
    # At most :max_pending held by the page at once: the rest is dropped.
    pending = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_pending_messages, 0)
    {sent, dropped} = run.messages |> Enum.reverse() |> Enum.split(max(max_pending() - pending, 0))
    socket = assign(socket, :bubble_pending_messages, pending + length(sent))
    n = max(length(sent), 1)
    budget = %{jobs: div(run.jobs, n), calls: div(run.calls, n), chain: run.chain + 1}

    for message <- sent do
      case message do
        {delay, {:resume, frames, now}} ->
          Process.send_after(self(), {:bubble, :resume, frames, now, budget}, delay)

        {delay, scope, module, id, args} ->
          Process.send_after(self(), {:bubble, :run, scope, module, id, args, budget}, delay)
      end
    end

    if dropped == [] do
      socket
    else
      Logger.warning(
        "bubble: #{length(dropped)} paused or scheduled workflow(s) dropped: " <>
          "the page already holds :max_pending (#{max_pending()})"
      )

      push_event(socket, "bubble:notice", %{text: @refused_notice})
    end
  end

  defp ctx(socket, module, scope, run) do
    actor = <%= if @enforced? do %>current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>
    root = Runtime.root(nil, actor)
    backend = %{root | budget: run.jobs, calls: run.calls, chain: run.chain}

    %Ctx{
      module: module,
      scope: scope,
      actor: actor,
      backend: backend,
      now: DateTime.utc_now(),
      states: socket.assigns.bubble_states,
      inputs: socket.assigns.bubble_inputs,
      first: socket.assigns.bubble_first_inputs,
      url: socket.assigns.bubble_url,
      path: socket.assigns.bubble_path,
      page_path: Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_page_path, socket.assigns.bubble_path),
      takes_thing: Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_takes_thing, false),
      data: Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data, %{}),
      displayed: Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_displayed, %{}),
      thing: Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_thing)
    }
  end

  @doc """
  The context a page's data source runs with (`<%= @web %>.BubbleData`):
  the page's state, what it loaded so far (`data`) and, in a repeating
  group's cell, `{thing, index}`.
  """
  def data_ctx(socket, module, scope, data, cell \\ nil) do
    ctx = ctx(socket, module, scope, start(socket, nil))
    ctx = %{ctx | data: data}

    case cell do
      {item, index} -> %{ctx | cell: item, cell_index: index}
      nil -> ctx
    end
  end

  # Runs workflows `ids` of `module` in `scope` with what is left of the
  # event's budgets; returns the socket and the event's run, charged.
  defp run_event(socket, module, scope, ids, args, run) do
    {ctx, refused?} =
      Enum.reduce(ids, {ctx(socket, module, scope, run), false}, fn id, {ctx, refused?} ->
        {status, ctx} = run(ctx, module, id, args, scope)
        {paused(ctx, status), refused? or refused?(status)}
      end)

    socket = if refused?, do: assign(socket, :bubble_refused, true), else: socket
    finish(socket, ctx, run)
  end

  # The rest of a paused workflow and of the custom events waiting on it
  # (WTF-451), with the start time it had, on the budgets the pause left.
  defp resume_event(socket, [frame | _] = frames, now, run) do
    ctx = %{ctx(socket, frame.module, frame.scope, run) | now: now}
    {status, ctx} = resume(ctx, frames)
    finish(socket, paused(ctx, status), run)
  end

  defp finish(socket, ctx, run) do
    b = backend(ctx)
    run = %{run | jobs: b.budget, calls: b.calls, messages: ctx.messages ++ run.messages}
    {apply_ctx(socket, ctx), run}
  end

  # A paused workflow's rest is sent when the event ends, after the pause.
  defp paused(ctx, {:paused, ms, frames}),
    do: %{ctx | messages: [{ms, {:resume, frames, ctx.now}} | ctx.messages]}

  defp paused(ctx, _status), do: ctx

  # Refused before its first step: not lowered, or data access is off.
  defp refused?({:error, {:not_lowered, _}}), do: true
  defp refused?({:error, {:data_access_disabled, _}}), do: true
  defp refused?(_status), do: false

  defp apply_ctx(socket, %Ctx{} = ctx) do
    # A data step may have written what the page shows; a custom state or
    # an input may be a search constraint (an input only for the sources
    # reading it, WTF-475); a display step (or a reset) changes what an
    # element shows (WTF-492).
    changed = changed_inputs(socket.assigns.bubble_inputs, ctx.inputs)
    displayed = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_displayed, %{})

    socket =
      cond do
        ctx.data_stale or ctx.states != socket.assigns.bubble_states or
            ctx.displayed != displayed ->
          BubbleData.mark_stale(socket)

        changed != [] ->
          BubbleData.mark_inputs(socket, Enum.map(changed, &elem(&1, 1)))

        true ->
          socket
      end

    # A value a workflow sets (a reset) is not the user's change: the next
    # commit compares with it.
    committed =
      Enum.reduce(changed, Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_committed) || %{}, fn key, acc ->
        Map.put(acc, key, Map.get(ctx.inputs, key))
      end)

    socket =
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_states, ctx.states)
      |> assign(:bubble_inputs, ctx.inputs)
      |> assign(:bubble_displayed, ctx.displayed)
      |> assign(:bubble_committed, committed)

    socket =
      if ctx.js == [],
        do: socket,
        else: push_event(socket, "bubble:exec", %{ops: Enum.reverse(ctx.js)})

    apply_navigation(socket, ctx.navigate)
  end

  # The workflows of one event apply their navigation as each ends
  # (WTF-500), and LiveView raises on a second redirect of one socket. The
  # first page-leaving navigation (another page, a reload, a URL, log out)
  # wins: in Bubble the page is gone once it runs, and Bubble does not
  # guarantee the order of workflows on the same trigger, so neither does
  # this. A same-page one (`:patch`, a URL parameter) never blocks: a later
  # navigation of any kind replaces it, so changing a parameter can never
  # skip a "Log out".
  defp apply_navigation(socket, nil), do: socket

  defp apply_navigation(%{redirected: redirected} = socket, to) do
    if leaves_page?(redirected) do
      Logger.debug(
        "bubble: a later navigation of the same event is ignored: #{inspect(to)} (first: #{inspect(redirected)})"
      )

      socket
    else
      # An earlier same-page patch (or none) gives way.
      navigate_now(%{socket | redirected: nil}, to)
    end
  end

  defp navigate_now(socket, to) do
    case to do
      {:patch, to, replace?} -> push_patch(socket, to: to, replace: replace?)
      {:navigate, to, replace?} -> push_navigate(socket, to: to, replace: replace?)
      {:redirect, to} -> redirect(socket, to: to)
      {:external, url} -> redirect(socket, external: url)
    end
  end

  # The inputs (`{scope, element}`) whose value differs between `before`
  # and `now`.
  defp changed_inputs(same, same), do: []

  defp changed_inputs(before, now) do
    (Map.keys(before) ++ Map.keys(now))
    |> Enum.uniq()
    |> Enum.filter(&(Map.get(before, &1) != Map.get(now, &1)))
  end

  # Condition-true workflows: each runs when its condition becomes true
  # (once per page load for `:once`); their effects may make others true,
  # so it repeats, at most @max_rounds times. They run within the event's
  # `run` (its budgets and chain), never a fresh root.
  defp settle(socket, page, run, round \\ 0) do
    seen = socket.assigns.bubble_conditions

    # One read pass (`BubbleData.read_pass/1`): checking conditions writes
    # nothing, so what they read of the current user is read once.
    {fire, seen} =
      BubbleData.read_pass(fn -> fire(socket, page, seen) end)

    socket = assign(socket, :bubble_conditions, seen)
    settle_fired(socket, page, run, round, fire)
  end

  # The condition-true workflows to run now (`settle/4`), and what each
  # condition is.
  defp fire(socket, page, seen) do
    for {scope, module} <- surfaces(page),
        {id, run_when} <- module.__bubble__(:surface).conditions,
        reduce: {[], seen} do
      {fire, seen} ->
        key = {scope, id}
        now = condition?(socket, module, scope, id)
        before = Map.get(seen, key, %{now: false, ran: false})

        if now and not before.now and not (run_when == :once and before.ran),
          do: {[{scope, module, id} | fire], Map.put(seen, key, %{now: true, ran: true})},
          else: {fire, Map.put(seen, key, %{before | now: now})}
    end
  end

  defp settle_fired(socket, page, run, round, fire) do
    cond do
      fire == [] ->
        {socket, run}

      round >= @max_rounds ->
        Logger.warning("bubble: condition-true workflows keep firing; stopped after #{@max_rounds} rounds")
        {socket, run}

      true ->
        {socket, run} =
          fire
          |> Enum.reverse()
          |> Enum.reduce({socket, run}, fn {scope, module, id}, {socket, run} ->
            run_event(socket, module, scope, [id], %{}, run)
          end)

        # A fired workflow can change a source or its constraints. Keep the
        # same run budgets while re-reading (when stale) before the next
        # condition check.
        settle(BubbleData.reload(socket, page), page, run, round + 1)
    end
  end

  defp condition?(socket, module, scope, id) do
    with %{condition: fun, blocked: [], data: data} when is_atom(fun) and fun != nil <-
           module.__bubble__(:workflows)[id],
         true <- not data or data_access?() do
      apply(module, fun, [ctx(socket, module, scope, start(socket, nil))]) == true
    else
      _ -> false
    end
  end

  # --- running a workflow -------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Runs workflow `id` of `module` in instance `scope` with `args` (a custom
  event's parameters by ID). Returns `{status, ctx}`: `:done`, `:not_run`
  (its condition was false), `:terminated` or `{:error, reason}`; `ctx`
  carries its effects.
  """
  def run(%Ctx{} = ctx, module, id, args \\ %{}, scope \\ nil) do
    scope = scope || ctx.scope

    case module.__bubble__(:workflows)[id] do
      nil ->
        {{:error, {:unknown_workflow, id}}, ctx}

      %{run: nil} ->
        {{:error, {:runs_in_browser, id}}, ctx}

      meta ->
        ctx = %{ctx | backend: ctx.backend || Runtime.root(id, ctx.actor)}

        cond do
          meta.blocked != [] ->
            Logger.error(
              "bubble workflow #{inspect(id)} is not lowered (#{inspect(meta.blocked)}); no step ran"
            )

            {{:error, {:not_lowered, meta.blocked}}, ctx}

          meta.data and not data_access?() ->
            Logger.error(
              "bubble workflow #{inspect(id)} not run: it reads or writes stored data and " <>
                "data access is off (config :<%= @app %>, #{inspect(__MODULE__)}, data_access: true)"
            )

            {{:error, {:data_access_disabled, id}}, ctx}

          ctx.depth >= @max_depth ->
            {{:error, {:depth_limit, id}}, ctx}

          true ->
            child = %{
              ctx
              | module: module,
                workflow: id,
                scope: scope,
                args: args,
                steps: %{},
                returns: nil,
                depth: ctx.depth + 1
            }

            {status, child} = apply(module, meta.run, [child])
            back = %{child | module: ctx.module, workflow: ctx.workflow, scope: ctx.scope}
            {status, %{back | args: ctx.args, steps: ctx.steps, depth: ctx.depth}}
        end
    end
  end

  defp data_access?,
    do: Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :data_access) == true

  @doc """
  Runs `steps` (functions of the context answering `{:cont, ctx}` or
  `{:halt, status, ctx}`) when `condition` (nil, or a function of the
  context) holds. A paused workflow (`ctx.resume`, WTF-451) continues
  from the step after its pause: its condition held when it started.
  A pause ends the run with `{:paused, ms, frames}`: what to continue,
  the innermost workflow first.
  """
  def steps(%Ctx{resume: n} = ctx, _condition, steps) when is_integer(n) and n > 0,
    do: run_steps(%{ctx | resume: nil}, Enum.drop(steps, n - 1), n)

  def steps(ctx, condition, steps) do
    if condition == nil or condition.(ctx) == true,
      do: run_steps(ctx, steps, 1),
      else: {:not_run, ctx}
  end

  defp run_steps(ctx, steps, first) do
    steps
    |> Enum.with_index(first)
    |> Enum.reduce_while({:done, ctx}, fn {step, n}, {_status, ctx} ->
      case step.(ctx) do
        {:cont, ctx} ->
          {:cont, {:done, ctx}}

        # Paused here, or in a custom event step `call` waits on.
        {:halt, {:pause, ms, frames, call}, ctx} ->
          {:halt, {{:paused, ms, frames ++ [frame(ctx, n + 1, call)]}, ctx}}

        {:halt, status, ctx} ->
          {:halt, {status, ctx}}
      end
    end)
  end

  # What a paused workflow continues with: the step after the pause and,
  # when it waits on a custom event, the step that gets its return values.
  defp frame(ctx, at, call) do
    %{
      module: ctx.module,
      workflow: ctx.workflow,
      scope: ctx.scope,
      args: ctx.args,
      steps: ctx.steps,
      returns: ctx.returns,
      at: at,
      call: call
    }
  end

  @doc """
  "Add a pause before next action" (WTF-451): `length` milliseconds (at
  most `:max_pause_ms`; empty or negative is none). It costs one call and
  ends the run here; the page runs the rest after the pause, one link
  further down the chain (see the moduledoc).
  """
  def pause(ctx, step, length) do
    b = backend(ctx)

    cond do
      b.calls < 1 ->
        fail(ctx, step, {:call_budget_exhausted, ctx.workflow})

      b.chain >= max_chain() ->
        fail(ctx, step, {:chain_limit, ctx.workflow})

      true ->
        ctx = put_step(%{ctx | backend: %{b | calls: b.calls - 1}}, step, nil)
        {:halt, {:pause, pause_ms(length), [], nil}, ctx}
    end
  end

  @doc "A pause's length in milliseconds: `length` capped at `:max_pause_ms`."
  def pause_ms(length) when is_number(length) and length > 0,
    do: length |> round() |> min(max_pause_ms())

  def pause_ms(_length), do: 0

  defp max_pause_ms do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_pause_ms, 60_000) do
      ms when is_integer(ms) and ms >= 0 -> min(ms, 4_294_967_295)
      _ -> 60_000
    end
  end

  # Continues `frames` (innermost first): each workflow from the step after
  # its pause; when one ends, the custom event step waiting on it gets its
  # return values and its caller continues. A failure ends every caller
  # (as a failing custom event fails its call step); a new pause returns
  # what is still waiting.
  defp resume(ctx, [frame | outer]) do
    case continue(ctx, frame, length(outer)) do
      {{:paused, ms, frames}, ctx} ->
        {{:paused, ms, frames ++ outer}, ctx}

      {status, ctx} when outer == [] ->
        {status, ctx}

      {{:error, reason}, ctx} ->
        [caller | _] = outer
        Logger.warning("bubble workflow #{inspect(caller.workflow)}: step #{inspect(caller.call)} failed after a pause: #{inspect(reason)}")
        {{:error, {caller.call, reason}}, ctx}

      {_status, ctx} ->
        [caller | rest] = outer
        caller = %{caller | steps: Map.put(caller.steps, caller.call, ctx.returns)}
        resume(ctx, [caller | rest])
    end
  end

  defp continue(ctx, frame, depth) do
    case frame.module.__bubble__(:workflows)[frame.workflow] do
      %{run: fun, blocked: [], data: data} when is_atom(fun) and fun != nil ->
        if data and not data_access?() do
          {{:error, {:data_access_disabled, frame.workflow}}, ctx}
        else
          child = %{
            ctx
            | module: frame.module,
              workflow: frame.workflow,
              scope: frame.scope,
              args: frame.args,
              steps: frame.steps,
              returns: frame.returns,
              depth: depth + 1,
              resume: frame.at
          }

          apply(frame.module, fun, [child])
        end

      _ ->
        {{:error, {:not_resumable, frame.workflow}}, ctx}
    end
  end

  @doc "A step whose condition is false."
  def skip(ctx), do: {:cont, ctx}

  @doc "A step bubble_ex did not lower: never reached (the workflow refuses to start)."
  def not_lowered(ctx, step, type) do
    Logger.error("bubble workflow #{inspect(ctx.workflow)}: step #{inspect(step)} (#{inspect(type)}) is not lowered")
    {:halt, {:error, {:not_lowered, step, type}}, ctx}
  end

  # --- values ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc "The scope of the instance `path` (Bubble IDs) below the workflow's."
  def scope(ctx, path), do: Enum.reduce(path, ctx.scope, &Bubble.nest(&2, &1))

  @doc "Custom state `state` of `element` (in the instance `path` below)."
  def state(ctx, path, element, state), do: Map.get(ctx.states, {scope(ctx, path), element, state})

  @doc "The value of input `element` (in the instance `path` below)."
  def input(ctx, path, element), do: Map.get(ctx.inputs, {scope(ctx, path), element})

  @doc "URL parameter `name`, as text."
  def url(ctx, name), do: Map.get(ctx.url, name)

  @doc """
  What element `element` (in the instance `path` below) holds of the
  page's data (WTF-420): a page's, group's or instance's thing, a
  repeating group's list.
  """
  def data(ctx, path, element), do: Map.get(ctx.data, {scope(ctx, path), element})

  @doc "What group `element` holds in the current cell of a repeating group."
  def cell_data(ctx, element), do: Map.get(ctx.data, {ctx.scope, element, ctx.cell_index})

  @doc "A custom event's parameter."
  def param(ctx, id, loads), do: ctx.args |> Map.get(id) |> load(loads, ctx)

  @doc "The result of an earlier step."
  def step(ctx, action, loads), do: ctx.steps |> Map.get(action) |> load(loads, ctx)

  @doc """
  The current user, with `loads`. While the page checks its conditions
  (`settle/4`, nothing written meanwhile) the same loads are read once
  for all of them (`BubbleData.once/3`, WTF-501).
  """
  def actor(ctx, []), do: ctx.actor

  def actor(ctx, loads) do
    key = {:workflow_actor, Enum.sort(loads), backend(ctx).authorize?}
    BubbleData.once(key, ctx.actor, fn -> load(ctx.actor, loads, ctx) end)
  end

  @doc "`value` with the relationship `loads` loaded (`Runtime.load/3`)."
  #
  # Fails closed: with data access off it reads nothing and answers nil
  # (the workflow's `data` flag should have stopped it before; this is the
  # second lock).
  def load(value, [], _ctx), do: value

  def load(value, loads, ctx) do
    if data_access?() do
      Runtime.load(value, loads, backend(ctx))
    else
      Logger.error("bubble workflow #{inspect(ctx.workflow)}: a load with data access off; nothing read")
      nil
    end
  end

  defp backend(ctx), do: %{(ctx.backend || Runtime.root(ctx.workflow, ctx.actor)) | actor: ctx.actor}

  # --- element and state steps --------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc "Show / hide / toggle / focus / scroll to / reset an element (`nil`: the instance root)."
  def element(ctx, op, path, element) do
    {:cont, %{ctx | js: [%{op: op, to: Bubble.selector(scope(ctx, path), element)} | ctx.js]}}
  end

  @doc """
  Reset inputs back to their first values: those of element `within`
  (`inputs`, the ones the surface lists there), or with nil every input of
  the instance or page, its nested instances' included. A reset group or
  popup also forgets what "Display data" steps showed in it and in the
  elements inside it (`clears`, WTF-492; in every cell); a reset instance
  (`clears: :all`) everything they showed in its scope. The elements then show their own
  data source again, or nothing.
  """
  def reset(ctx, path, within, inputs, clears \\ []) do
    scope = scope(ctx, path)

    displayed =
      case clears do
        :all ->
          Map.reject(ctx.displayed, fn {key, _} -> within?(elem(key, 0), scope) end)

        clears ->
          Map.reject(ctx.displayed, fn {key, _} ->
            elem(key, 0) == scope and elem(key, 1) in clears
          end)
      end

    ctx = %{ctx | displayed: displayed}
    to = if within == nil and scope == "", do: "body", else: Bubble.selector(scope, within)

    values =
      if within == nil,
        do:
          Map.merge(
            ctx.inputs,
            Map.filter(ctx.first, fn {{s, _element}, _} -> within?(s, scope) end)
          ),
        else:
          Enum.reduce(inputs, ctx.inputs, fn {element, first}, acc ->
            Map.put(acc, {scope, element}, first)
          end)

    {:cont, %{ctx | inputs: values, js: [%{op: "reset", to: to} | ctx.js]}}
  end

  defp within?(_scope, ""), do: true
  defp within?(scope, scope), do: true
  defp within?(scope, outer), do: String.starts_with?(scope, outer <> "-")

  @doc "Set state(s): `states` are `{path, element, state, value}`."
  def set_state(ctx, step, states) do
    values =
      Enum.reduce(states, ctx.states, fn {path, element, state, value}, acc ->
        Map.put(acc, {scope(ctx, path), element, state}, value)
      end)

    {:cont, put_step(%{ctx | states: values}, step, nil)}
  end

  @doc """
  "Display data in a group / popup" or "Display list in a repeating group"
  (WTF-492): element `element` (in the instance `path` below; in the
  current cell when `cell?`, keyed by the cell's thing, not its position)
  shows `value` until a reset or the page's next load, in place of its
  own data source.

  With a `resource`, only unique IDs are kept: a record of `resource` as
  its ID, a text shaped like a Bubble ID as itself; anything else (a
  record of another type, a crafted text, a number) is dropped, and a
  list keeps at most `page_size` (capped by `:max_items`) of them. Every
  read of the page's data reads them again through Ash as the current
  user (`<%= @web %>.BubbleData`), so a workflow never shows what the user
  may not read, only what the policies let the user read at that moment.
  Without a resource the value (text, a number, a date) is kept as it is,
  never a record.

  The workflow's later steps read the element's new data at once: it is
  read the same way, as the current user, into the context (nothing with
  data access off).
  """
  def display(ctx, step, path, element, cell?, resource, list?, value, page_size \\ nil) do
    scope = scope(ctx, path)

    keys =
      cond do
        not cell? -> {:ok, {scope, element}, {scope, element}}
        ctx.cell != nil -> {:ok, {scope, element, {:cell, Runtime.id(ctx.cell)}}, {scope, element, ctx.cell_index}}
        true -> :error
      end

    case keys do
      {:ok, key, data_key} ->
        shown = {resource, list?, displayed_value(resource, list?, value, page_size)}

        ctx = %{
          ctx
          | displayed: Map.put(ctx.displayed, key, shown),
            data: Map.put(ctx.data, data_key, BubbleData.show(ctx, shown, page_size))
        }

        {:cont, put_step(ctx, step, nil)}

      :error ->
        fail(ctx, step, :not_in_cell)
    end
  end

  defp displayed_value(nil, true, value, page_size),
    do: value |> List.wrap() |> plain() |> Enum.take(BubbleData.cap(page_size))

  defp displayed_value(nil, false, value, _page_size), do: plain(value)

  defp displayed_value(resource, true, value, page_size),
    do:
      value
      |> List.wrap()
      |> Enum.map(&displayed_id(resource, &1))
      |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
      |> Enum.take(BubbleData.cap(page_size))

  defp displayed_value(resource, false, value, _page_size), do: displayed_id(resource, value)

  # A thing's unique ID: a record of `resource`, or a text shaped like a
  # Bubble ID. Never a record of another type, nor another value.
  defp displayed_id(resource, %{__struct__: resource} = record), do: bubble_id(Runtime.id(record))
  defp displayed_id(_resource, %{__struct__: _}), do: nil
  defp displayed_id(_resource, id), do: bubble_id(id)

  defp bubble_id(id) when is_binary(id), do: if(BubbleData.bubble_id?(id), do: id)
  defp bubble_id(_id), do: nil

  # A value shown as it is: never a record (a struct), which only the
  # resource's re-read may show.
  defp plain(%{__struct__: module} = value) when module in [Date, DateTime, NaiveDateTime, Time, Decimal],
    do: value

  defp plain(%{__struct__: _}), do: nil
  defp plain(list) when is_list(list), do: list |> Enum.map(&plain/1) |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
  defp plain(%{} = map), do: Map.new(map, fn {k, v} -> {k, plain(v)} end)
  defp plain(value), do: value

  # --- navigation -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Go to page `to` (a path, or `:current`) with `params` (`{key, value}`,
  shown as text), keeping the current ones when `keep?`. `thing`, the
  data to send, is the path segment after the page's own (`/index/<...>`
  for the index page, WTF-454):

    * to a page with a type of content, a record (or its unique ID): its
      unique ID; an empty one (or a value that is not a thing's ID) sends
      nothing;
    * `{:segment, value}`, to a page with no type of content (WTF-466,
      as Bubble does): a record's unique ID, else the value (text, a
      number, a boolean or a date) as text, percent-encoded as one
      segment; an empty one, `.` or `..`, any other value (a list
      included) or one over 2000 encoded bytes (logged) sends nothing.

  Sent to the current page (WTF-454), it replaces the segment of the
  page's URL: a thing's unique ID when the page takes a thing, else as
  `{:segment, value}`.
  """
  def navigate(ctx, to, params, keep?, replace?, new_tab?, thing \\ :none) do
    path =
      case {to, segment(ctx, to, thing)} do
        {:current, nil} when thing == :none -> ctx.path
        {:current, nil} -> ctx.page_path
        {:current, segment} -> thing_path(ctx.page_path, segment)
        {page, nil} -> page
        {page, segment} -> thing_path(page, segment)
      end

    base = if keep?, do: ctx.url, else: %{}

    query =
      Enum.reduce(params, base, fn {key, value}, acc ->
        case <%= @module %>.Bubble.Runtime.text(value) do
          "" -> Map.delete(acc, key)
          text -> Map.put(acc, key, text)
        end
      end)

    url = if query == %{}, do: path, else: path <> "?" <> URI.encode_query(query)

    cond do
      new_tab? -> {:cont, %{ctx | js: [%{op: "open", url: url} | ctx.js]}}
      to == :current or path == ctx.path -> {:cont, navigation(ctx, {:patch, url, replace?})}
      true -> {:cont, navigation(ctx, {:navigate, url, replace?})}
    end
  end

  # The path segment of the data sent: none, a thing's unique ID, or (to a
  # page with no type of content) any value as one encoded segment.
  defp segment(_ctx, _to, :none), do: nil
  defp segment(_ctx, _to, {:segment, value}), do: text_segment(value)
  defp segment(%Ctx{takes_thing: false}, :current, value), do: text_segment(value)
  defp segment(_ctx, _to, value), do: thing_id(value)

  # At most this many bytes of encoded segment; a longer one sends none.
  @max_segment 2000

  # Text, a number, a boolean, a date or a record (its unique ID); any
  # other value (a list, a map without an ID…) sends none, never debug
  # output. Only unreserved characters stay as they are: never a `/`, `?`,
  # `#`, backslash or `%` of its own, so never another path, host or page;
  # `.` and `..` (which browsers resolve, even percent-encoded) send nothing.
  defp text_segment(value) do
    case segment_text(value) do
      text when text in [nil, "", ".", ".."] ->
        nil

      text ->
        case URI.encode(text, &URI.char_unreserved?/1) do
          encoded when byte_size(encoded) <= @max_segment ->
            encoded

          encoded ->
            Logger.warning(
              "bubble: data sent to a page is #{byte_size(encoded)} bytes encoded (over #{@max_segment}); sent no path segment"
            )

            nil
        end
    end
  end

  defp segment_text(%{id: id}) when is_binary(id) or is_integer(id), do: to_string(id)

  defp segment_text(value)
       when is_binary(value) or is_number(value) or is_boolean(value) or is_struct(value, Decimal) or
              is_struct(value, Date) or is_struct(value, DateTime) or
              is_struct(value, NaiveDateTime),
       do: <%= @module %>.Bubble.Runtime.text(value)

  defp segment_text(_value), do: nil

  # A page's path with its thing's segment: never "//<id>" (a
  # scheme-relative URL); the index page's is under /index.
  defp thing_path(page, id) do
    case String.trim_trailing(page, "/") do
      "" -> "/index/" <> id
      base -> base <> "/" <> id
    end
  end

  defp thing_id(%{id: id}), do: thing_id(id)

  defp thing_id(id) when is_binary(id),
    do: if(Regex.match?(~r/\A[0-9]{1,20}x[0-9]{1,24}\z/, id), do: id)

  defp thing_id(_), do: nil

  @doc "Open an external website: an http(s) URL or a path of this site; anything else fails the step."
  def open_url(ctx, step, url, new_tab?) do
    case safe_url(url) do
      nil ->
        fail(ctx, step, {:unsafe_url, url})

      {kind, url} ->
        cond do
          new_tab? -> {:cont, %{ctx | js: [%{op: "open", url: url} | ctx.js]}}
          kind == :path -> {:cont, navigation(ctx, {:redirect, url})}
          true -> {:cont, navigation(ctx, {:external, url})}
        end
    end
  end

  # Backslashes and control characters are refused outright (browsers read
  # `/\\host` as `//host`), as LiveView's own redirect does.
  defp safe_url(url) when is_binary(url) do
    url = String.trim(url)
    uri = URI.parse(url)

    cond do
      String.contains?(url, "\\") or String.match?(url, ~r/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/) ->
        nil

      uri.scheme in ["http", "https"] and is_binary(uri.host) and uri.host != "" ->
        {:external, URI.to_string(uri)}

      uri.scheme == nil and uri.host == nil and is_binary(uri.path) and
          String.starts_with?(uri.path, "/") and not String.starts_with?(uri.path, "//") ->
        {:path, URI.to_string(uri)}

      true ->
        nil
    end
  end

  defp safe_url(_url), do: nil

  @doc "Refresh the page (a full reload)."
  def refresh(ctx) do
    to = if ctx.url == %{}, do: ctx.path, else: ctx.path <> "?" <> URI.encode_query(ctx.url)
    {:cont, navigation(ctx, {:redirect, to})}
  end

  @doc "Log the user out (the sign-out route)."
  def log_out(ctx), do: {:cont, navigation(ctx, {:redirect, "/sign-out"})}

  # A step's navigation (WTF-500): a page-leaving one (another page, a
  # reload, a URL, log out) is never replaced, by a later step or a later
  # workflow of the same event; a same-page one (`:patch`, a URL parameter)
  # is replaced by any later one. So "change a parameter" never cancels a
  # "Log out" or a "Go to page", whichever runs first.
  defp navigation(%Ctx{navigate: current} = ctx, to) do
    if leaves_page?(current), do: ctx, else: %{ctx | navigate: to}
  end

  # Page-leaving: a step's `{:navigate, _, _}`, `{:redirect, _}` or
  # `{:external, _}`, and a socket's `redirected` from them (LiveView's
  # `{:live, :redirect, _}` or `{:redirect, _}`); `:patch` stays.
  defp leaves_page?({kind, _}) when kind in [:redirect, :external], do: true
  defp leaves_page?({:navigate, _, _}), do: true
  defp leaves_page?({:live, :redirect, _}), do: true
  defp leaves_page?(_navigation), do: false

  # --- custom events ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Trigger custom event `id` of `module` in instance `path` below, now, with
  `args`; its return values are the step's result.
  """
  def call(ctx, step, module, id, path, args) do
    b = backend(ctx)

    if b.calls < 1 do
      fail(ctx, step, {:call_budget_exhausted, id})
    else
      called(%{ctx | backend: %{b | calls: b.calls - 1}}, step, module, id, path, args)
    end
  end

  defp called(ctx, step, module, id, path, args) do
    case run(ctx, module, id, args, scope(ctx, path)) do
      {{:error, reason}, after_call} ->
        fail(%{after_call | returns: ctx.returns}, step, reason)

      # The custom event paused (WTF-451): this workflow waits on it.
      {{:paused, ms, frames}, after_call} ->
        {:halt, {:pause, ms, frames, step}, %{after_call | returns: ctx.returns}}

      {_status, after_call} ->
        {:cont, put_step(%{after_call | returns: ctx.returns}, step, after_call.returns)}
    end
  end

  @doc """
  Schedule custom event `id` of `module` `delay` seconds from now (in this
  page). It costs one call of the run's call budget and continues the run's
  budgets (shared among what the run schedules); a chain of scheduled runs
  stops at `:max_chain` (`<%= @module %>.Workflows` config, default 10000) or
  when the budget is spent, so a self-scheduling event never spins forever.
  """
  def schedule_custom(ctx, step, module, id, path, delay, args) do
    b = backend(ctx)

    cond do
      b.calls < 1 ->
        fail(ctx, step, {:call_budget_exhausted, id})

      b.chain >= max_chain() ->
        fail(ctx, step, {:chain_limit, id})

      true ->
        ms = if is_number(delay) and delay > 0, do: clamp(delay, 0), else: 0
        entry = {ms, scope(ctx, path), module, id, args}
        ctx = %{ctx | backend: %{b | calls: b.calls - 1}, messages: [entry | ctx.messages]}
        {:cont, put_step(ctx, step, nil)}
    end
  end

  defp max_chain do
    Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, <%= @module %>.Workflows, []), :max_chain, 10_000)
  end

  # Seconds as milliseconds, at least `least` and at most the longest
  # timer Erlang takes (about 49 days).
  defp clamp(seconds, least),
    do: seconds |> Kernel.*(1000) |> round() |> max(least) |> min(4_294_967_295)

  @doc "Terminate this workflow, returning `returns` (a custom event's values)."
  def terminate(ctx, returns), do: {:halt, :terminated, %{ctx | returns: returns}}

  # --- data steps and backend workflows -------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Runs a step on the backend workflow runtime: `fun` gets its context
  (this event's budgets, the actor, the step results) and calls
  `Runtime.create/4`, `update/5`, `update_list/5`, `delete/3`,
  `delete_list/3`, `schedule/5` or `schedule_list/7`. It marks the page's
  data stale (a create, change or delete, even one that failed part-way,
  may have written what the page shows), so the page reads again before
  its next workflow or condition.
  """
  def backend(ctx, fun) do
    if data_access?(), do: run_backend(ctx, fun), else: {:halt, {:error, :data_access_disabled}, ctx}
  end

  defp run_backend(ctx, fun) do
    b = %{backend(ctx) | workflow: ctx.workflow, now: ctx.now, steps: ctx.steps}
    ctx = %{ctx | data_stale: true}

    case fun.(b) do
      {:cont, b} -> {:cont, %{ctx | backend: b, steps: b.steps}}
      {:halt, {:error, reason}} -> {:halt, {:error, reason}, ctx}
      {:halt, other} -> {:halt, {:error, {:unexpected, other}}, ctx}
    end
  end

  defp put_step(ctx, step, value), do: %{ctx | steps: Map.put(ctx.steps, step, value)}


  defp fail(ctx, step, reason) do
    Logger.warning("bubble workflow #{inspect(ctx.workflow)}: step #{inspect(step)} failed: #{inspect(reason)}")
    {:halt, {:error, {step, reason}}, ctx}
  end
end
